Since you need **three** themes, use the **ResourceDictionary swap** approach (`AppThemeBinding` only supports two). Here's the full setup:

---

## 1. Create three theme dictionaries

Each file needs matching `x:Key` values. Create under a `Themes/` folder:

**LightTheme.xaml**
```xml
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
                    x:Class="MyApp.Themes.LightTheme">
    <Color x:Key="PageBackgroundColor">White</Color>
    <Color x:Key="PrimaryTextColor">#333333</Color>
    <Color x:Key="AccentColor">#2196F3</Color>
    <Color x:Key="CardBackgroundColor">#F5F5F5</Color>
</ResourceDictionary>
```

**DarkTheme.xaml**
```xml
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
                    x:Class="MyApp.Themes.DarkTheme">
    <Color x:Key="PageBackgroundColor">#121212</Color>
    <Color x:Key="PrimaryTextColor">#EEEEEE</Color>
    <Color x:Key="AccentColor">#BB86FC</Color>
    <Color x:Key="CardBackgroundColor">#1E1E1E</Color>
</ResourceDictionary>
```

**HighContrastTheme.xaml**
```xml
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
                    x:Class="MyApp.Themes.HighContrastTheme">
    <Color x:Key="PageBackgroundColor">Black</Color>
    <Color x:Key="PrimaryTextColor">White</Color>
    <Color x:Key="AccentColor">Yellow</Color>
    <Color x:Key="CardBackgroundColor">#1A1A1A</Color>
</ResourceDictionary>
```

Each needs a code-behind:
```csharp
namespace MyApp.Themes;
public partial class LightTheme : ResourceDictionary
{
    public LightTheme() => InitializeComponent();
}
// Repeat for DarkTheme and HighContrastTheme
```

## 2. Theme switcher service

```csharp
public static class ThemeService
{
    public static void ApplyTheme(string themeName)
    {
        ResourceDictionary theme = themeName switch
        {
            "Dark"         => new DarkTheme(),
            "HighContrast" => new HighContrastTheme(),
            _              => new LightTheme()
        };

        var merged = Application.Current!.Resources.MergedDictionaries;
        merged.Clear();
        merged.Add(theme);

        // Persist the choice
        Preferences.Set("AppTheme", themeName);
    }

    public static void ApplySavedTheme()
    {
        var saved = Preferences.Get("AppTheme", "Light");
        ApplyTheme(saved);
    }
}
```

## 3. Apply on startup (`App.xaml.cs`)

```csharp
public App()
{
    InitializeComponent();
    ThemeService.ApplySavedTheme();
}
```

## 4. Settings page with a Picker

```xml
<ContentPage BackgroundColor="{DynamicResource PageBackgroundColor}">
    <VerticalStackLayout Padding="20">
        <Label Text="Choose Theme"
               TextColor="{DynamicResource PrimaryTextColor}" />
        <Picker x:Name="ThemePicker"
                SelectedIndexChanged="OnThemeChanged">
            <Picker.ItemsSource>
                <x:Array Type="{x:Type x:String}">
                    <x:String>Light</x:String>
                    <x:String>Dark</x:String>
                    <x:String>HighContrast</x:String>
                </x:Array>
            </Picker.ItemsSource>
        </Picker>
    </VerticalStackLayout>
</ContentPage>
```

```csharp
protected override void OnAppearing()
{
    base.OnAppearing();
    var saved = Preferences.Get("AppTheme", "Light");
    ThemePicker.SelectedItem = saved;
}

void OnThemeChanged(object sender, EventArgs e)
{
    if (ThemePicker.SelectedItem is string theme)
        ThemeService.ApplyTheme(theme);
}
```

## 5. Use `DynamicResource` everywhere

```xml
<!-- ✅ Will update instantly on theme switch -->
<Label TextColor="{DynamicResource PrimaryTextColor}" />

<!-- ❌ StaticResource won't update at runtime -->
<Label TextColor="{StaticResource PrimaryTextColor}" />
```

## Key reminders

- **Every `x:Key` must exist in all three dictionaries** — a missing key silently falls back to defaults.
- **Android**: ensure `MainActivity` includes `ConfigChanges.UiMode` to avoid activity restarts on OS theme changes.
- **CSS themes can't be swapped at runtime** — stick with ResourceDictionary.
